Z||000010||fropuff||06-20-2000||12:13 PM||||I'm very sorry to hear that doughboy. There is a couple of kids in my grade that got pulled over for illegal driving, and none of them had their licenses. The driver had a warrant on him for running away, and he was 15. Everyone else was 15, and the cops saw that and nabbed them. None of them can drive till they're 18! That's their fault though. Still as bad as a $5000 fine. I think that's a little harsh. Oh, I'm getting my car painted; had to take off the fascia plate. What I do is stick the plate in the wipers when they're down, then cover up the tabs with the wipers. (May 2000). On the back, I turned my plate frame upside down. I'm not condoning this; just an idea.||||reg||4
